      "leadSummary": "Exhaustive treatment of the two-nucleon bound system: deuteron ground state properties (J^π = 1⁺, B = 2.2245 MeV, I = 0), radial Schrödinger equation in central square well potentials, depth-radius relationship, absence of bound excited states and the ¹S₀ virtual level, non-zero electric quadrupole moment Q = +0.286 fm², non-central tensor force and ³S₁-³D₁ state mixing (η ≈ 0.0256), magnetic dipole moment discrepancy, root-mean-square radius (R_rms ≈ 2.14 fm), and photodisintegration kinematics and cross-sections (γ + d → n + p).",
